# Playbook Memory

State file for the Playbook brief. Maintained by the teacher skill: updated after every issue (what was taught, at what depth), every quiz and monthly test (verification results), and every Pulse scouting handoff (queue additions). Baseline established 2026-07-23 via the four-phase foundational interview.

## Reader baseline (interview summary)

Accounting graduate, corporate-finance fluent, operates a working agent system (this repo) built through Claude without technical background. Knowledge clusters on the usage side and the narrative side; the mechanical layer beneath both is largely absent. Two standing traits verified across all four phases:

- **Reasoning outruns vocabulary.** Repeatedly produced correct concepts he could not name (invented disintermediation logic while rating the term 0; articulated the reason–act–observe agent loop unprompted; reconstructed the vendor-financing circular-deal critique from memory). Lessons should bolt names and structure onto existing instincts, not build from zero.
- **Finance fluency has a precise boundary.** Statements-and-valuation fluent (gross margin, depreciation mechanics, balance-sheet reasoning, spread economics — all verified strong). Tech business-model taxonomy absent (SaaS metrics, moat types, take rates, payments, vertical SaaS — all 0–1). Finance frames are the preferred on-ramp for new material.

