### Misconception log
Each corrects inside its natural lesson, not as a standalone scolding.

| Misconception | Reality | Corrective lesson |
|---|---|---|
| Data centers sell storage; compute deals buy "storage space" | Compute is arithmetic capacity (chips-per-hour), storage is the filing cabinet | What Is Compute (keystone) |
| Tokens are units of energy/cost | Tokens are units of text; cost follows | Tokens & Context |
| Weights are "the algorithm" | Weights are the numbers; the program runs them | Model vs. Product vs. API |
| GPU = training, CPU = inference | Both run on GPUs; real split is parallel arithmetic vs. general sequencing | What Is Compute |
| Thin briefs = model rationing tokens | Context window filling; long-context degradation | Everything Is Text in Context |
| fetch script listens to podcast audio | Deterministic code fetching published transcripts; whisper transcription is separate and only for Bloomberg | Scripts vs. Models |
| Branch split was "a security protocol" | State accumulation (routine branch) vs. config stability (main) | What Git Actually Does |
| Paying for WSJ/Economist grants API access | Subscription = login; API = separate product, usually separate contract | APIs & Keys |
| Depreciation is "an accounting trick" | Real cost-matching; the live controversy is GPU useful-life assumptions vs. actual obsolescence | AI Capex & the Useful-Life Fight |
| ARR = annual run rate | Annual recurring revenue (run-rate is the adjacent, different concept) | SaaS Metrics |
| Clone-the-system = hand over repo + prompt | Repo is recipe; environment, subscription, secrets, schedule, keys are the kitchen | The Environment Layer |
| Amazon "not really building models" | Builds models (and holds the Anthropic stake); AWS-first frame otherwise sound | Big-Tech Decomposition |

