## Opening curriculum (sequenced; teacher skill selects per issue)

Prerequisite chains matter more than unit order — units interleave.

**Unit 1 — The Machine**
1. Model vs. Product vs. API (answers "would it look like ChatGPT"; unlocks open-weights questions)
2. Everything Is Text in Context (fuses the three partial insights; explains skills, CLAUDE.md, memory, thin briefs)
3. Tokens & Context (corrects energy misconception; builds on solid context intuition)
4. The Training Pipeline (slots his RLHF knowledge into pre-training → fine-tuning → RLHF)
5. Training vs. Inference Economics (capex/opex on-ramp; cost asymmetry)

**Unit 2 — The Agent** (requires 1.1–1.2)
Scripts vs. Models · Tool Calls & MCP · APIs & Keys · What Git Actually Does · The Environment Layer (clone-it lesson) · Loop Engineering (queued via Pulse scout, 2026-07; requires most of Unit 2)

**Unit 3 — The Physical Stack** (requires 1.5)
What Is Compute (keystone — the oil-barrel-to-model walk) · The Chip · The Foundry Chain (fab, nodes, EUV) · Data Center Anatomy (power + cooling) · Feeding the Engine (HBM + interconnect) · The Compute Market (hyperscalers, neoclouds, the deals, Oracle's role) · Powering It (grid, PPAs, gas, SMRs)

**Unit 4 — The Business** (requires 1.5; company decompositions require their layer's Unit 3 lessons where relevant)
Business-Model Taxonomy I: SaaS metrics · II: Vertical SaaS, marketplaces, payments · The Moat Audit (names his instincts) · The AI-Exposure Framework (becomes a standing lens) · The Seat Problem & the $20 Value Chain (the two blanks, taught not asked) · Lab Economics · The Wrapper Question

**Monthly decomposition syllabus** (proposed from interview evidence; standing veto): 1. Toast 2. Harvey 3. Nvidia

## North-star project
UHNW analyst agent (P2, Q34): portfolio-aware, prospectus-analyzing, no-trade agent for ultra-high-net-worth principals who have wealth managers but no analysts. Pedagogical capstone — requires model/API access, context vs. fine-tuning, document ingestion/RAG, output templating from exemplars, guardrails design. "Apply it" beats may advance it one step when material fits. Capability ranking from P4 Q33 weights all application: **buy / invest / operate > deal process**. Preferred application register: acquire → AI-nativize → cut cost.

